mlruns/
mlflow.db
*.json
!.mcp.json
# Test fixtures are pinned inputs, so they travel with the tests that read them.
# Licensed source blocks are stripped before anything lands here.
!tests/fixtures/*.json

# The labelled evaluation set. Published because the labels are the scarce part:
# most of them are analyst judgement the feeds do not supply, and an accuracy
# claim nobody can reproduce is not a measurement.
!tests/evaluation_set.json

# The domain training set is published so a clone can reproduce the model rather
# than be handed a pickle. Training is deterministic — random_state=42 throughout
# — and retraining from this file gives byte-identical predictions. The rest of
# data/ stays local: collection scratch, the 22MB Tranco list, the verdict log,
# and the IP sets, which are superseded.
data/*
!data/training_data_domains_v2.csv
!data/README.md
venv/
__pycache__/
.env
org_profile.yaml
ahmia_debug.html
.DS_Store
test_connectors.py

# Licensed source connectors — must never be published.
connectors/domaintools.py
connectors/dnsdb.py
core/tier.py

# Models stay local even now that the domain one is good. A .joblib is a pickle,
# so joblib.load() on a file from a pull request is arbitrary code execution, and
# a subtly retrained model is invisible to review in a way a CSV row is not.
# tests/test_domain_model.py skips rather than fails when none is installed.
models/*_domain.joblib
models/feature_columns_domain.joblib
